2>A useful first review.</h2><ol class="checklist"><li>Name the artifact and version.</li><li>State the exact hypotheses and scope.</li><li>Return proof notes, a counterexample, code or a reproduction receipt.</li><li>Distinguish what passed from what remains unresolved.</li><li>Agree attribution and publication of the review summary.</li></ol><p>A review of one result does not endorse the whole framework. Reviewer compensation, if separately agreed, is for careful work regardless of conclusion.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/issues/new">Offer a contribution on GitHub ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">Contribution workflow →</a></div></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>Starter tasks with high information value.</h2><div class="task-list"><div><b>01</b><p>Audit a declared A/B/C spectrum or fixed-mask continuity argument.</p></div><div><b>02</b><p>Review the receipt thermal-gap frontier, timing correction and dimensional non-identifiability proof.</p></div><div><b>03</b><p>Recover an original equation or scorer archive needed by a named open bridge.</p></div><div><b>04</b><p>Check the strict subdivision interface obstruction under its actual hypotheses.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">04</div><div><h2>Practical support.</h2><p>Compute access, suitable equipment, hosting, and support for a separately agreed independent review can help. No payment is collected through this site. The contribution guide provides the current process for coordinating a task.</p><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=R41">R41 · public contribution guide ↗</a></div></section></main><footer><div><a href="/">Unified Dynamics</a><p>Benjamin Walker Mayes · Independent researcher<br>AI-assisted research · Public reading edition 0.14</p></div><div><a href="/sources/">Sources & coverage</a><a href="