ref="/metric-admission/"><span>19</span>Source metrics</a><a href="/subdivision/"><span>20</span>Subdivision</a><a href="/metric-selection/"><span>21</span>Metric selection</a><a href="/refinement-tower/"><span>22</span>Refinement tower</a><a href="/history-comparison/"><span>23</span>History comparison</a><a href="/observation/"><span>24</span>Observation</a></nav><div class="sidebar-bottom"><span class="status-dot"></span> Physical promotion <b>0</b><p>Independent human review<br>pending</p><a href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD">Research repository ↗</a></div></aside><div class="page-shell"><header class="topbar"><span>FINITE STRUCTURE / OPEN CORRESPONDENCE</span><a href="/sources/">Search the record <span>⌕</span></a></header><main id="main"><div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">Evidence and physical correspondence</div><h1>A bridge is a specific test.</h1><p class="lede">No global physical identification is promoted. A mathematical agreement becomes a physical correspondence only through a declared map and independent evidence.</p></div><section class="chapter" id="observation-review-status"><div class="chapter-label">17 OCT</div><div><h2>The spectral certificates retain a review HOLD.</h2><p>The 600-cell session supplies exact finite proofs, conditional error bounds and frozen constructor benchmarks. It supplies no apparatus observations. Submitted non-constructor attestations do not bind to the archived package hashes or establish attributable independence; they remain on HOLD. Prior numerical certificates are preserved.</p><p>A lossless finite-history codec does not recover invisible bulk states. A count of 1893 singular values above a frozen threshold is not an exact-rank certificate. Repository publication does not change either boundary.</p><a class="text-link" href="/observation/#review">Review evidence and required return →</a></div></section><aside class="callout"><strong>Physical promotion: 0</strong><p>Finite proofs, exact replay, simulation, distribution and replication of an internal calculation have different evidentiary roles.</p></aside><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">01</div><div><h2>The evidence ladder.</h2><div class="ladder"><div><b>Internal mathematics</b><p>Proof or reproducible exact calculation on a declared carrier.</p></div><div><b>Candidate correspondence</b><p>Observable, measurement, units, calibration and uncertainty specified.</p></div><div><b>Frozen independent test</b><p>Inputs, baseline, exclusions and acceptance rule sealed before target exposure.</p></div><div><b>Replication and scoped ruling</b><p>Independent evaluation supports only the stated correspondence.</p></div></div><p>The supplied CRL-2 proposal distinguishes proposed, preregistered, executed and replicated measurement-facing objects. It requires a non-constructor review before advancement. The September 14 extension explicitly separates internal execution from measurement-facing CRL-2 execution.</p><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=A21">A21 · §§1–6 ↗</a> <a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=G14">G14 · §7.6 ↗</a></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">02</div><div><h2>Current physical frontiers.</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Frontier</th><th>Known boundary</th><th>Next discriminating input</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Pre-event polarity / POC-1</td><td>Frozen sidecar bytes and admissible native episode not recovered in the October 13 audit</td><td>Exact scorer archive plus independently authored, target-hidden native fixture</td></tr><tr><td>Lorentzian emergence</td><td>S₄ and preserved quadratic forms do not select a physical time direction</td><td>Source-selected refinement, principal symbol, common causal cone and clock map</td></tr><tr><td>Receipt entropy / area</td><td>Dimensionless errors do not identify physical area or energy cost</td><td>Native apparatus Hamiltonian, bath preparation, reset and geometric scale</td></tr><tr><td>LC operator bench</td><td>Prepared Stage 0 and estimator records; no measurement established here</td><td>Eligible calibrated capture and frozen comparison</td></tr><tr><td>Quadruple-tank correspondence</td><td>Delivered-flow source calibration and independent corpus are required</td><td>Source-authored calibration or directly measured pump flows</td></tr></tbody></table></div><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=R35">R35 · sidecar recovery ↗</a> <a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=R29">R29 · signature gates ↗</a> <a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=R40">R40 · source handoff ↗</a> <a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=M01">M01 · items 7–8 ↗</a></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>What “replicated” means in one recorded case.</h2><p>The portal records a Gemini replication and custodian CRL-2d ruling for the retained-parity carrier theorem: 12 in-scope passes and 6 failing controls. Its permanent rider is <em>transport consistency, not dynamical discovery</em>. This is source-recorded AI replication; it is not independent human review or a laboratory measurement.</p><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=GPAR">GPAR ↗</a> <a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=GREV">GREV ↗</a></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">04</div><div><h2>A physical bridge must expose its failure rule.</h2><ul class="checklist"><li>Typed mathematical observable and physical measurement</li><li>Units, calibration map and uncertainty budget</li><li>Null or baseline comparison</li><li>Frozen prediction, exclusions and acceptance threshold</li><li>Target custody, independent evaluation and negative-result reporting</li></ul><p>A result that fails its frozen criterion stays failed. Exploratory reanalysis gets a new version and requires fresh independent evaluation for confirmatory use.</p><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=G14">G14 · source and exact-launch gates ↗</a> <a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=PII">PII · §§8–9 ↗</a></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">05</div><div><h2>Applied programmes keep their own ledgers.</h2><div class="route-grid"><a href="https://mqm-research.ben-w-mayes.chatgpt.site"><span>QUANTUM CONTROL</span><h3>MQM</h3><p>Fault-aware quantum-code and controller research. No hardware advantage is asserted here.</p><b>Separate programme ↗</b></a><a href="https://voxifold-systems.ben-w-mayes.chatgpt.site"><span>SPATIAL COMPUTE</span><h3>Lattix Systems</h3><p>Inspectable spatial compute. Equal-recall, equal-hardware benchmarking remains a separate gate.</p><b>Separate programme ↗</b></a><a href="/sources/?q=TetraDEC"><span>PHOTONICS</span><h3>TetraDEC</h3><p>Historical computational and engineering proposals. Performance claims need their own benchmark evidence.</p><b>Find source records →</b></a></div><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=M01">M01 · applied programme crosswalk ↗</a></div></section></main><footer><div><a href="/">Unified Dynamics</a><p>Benjamin Walker Mayes · Independent researcher<br>AI-assisted research · Public reading edition 0.14</p></div><div><a href="/sources/">Sources & coverage</a><a href="/contribution/">Contribution</a><a href="https://tetrahedral-packet-complexes.ben-w-mayes.chatgpt.site/">Living research portal ↗</a></div><p class="footer-rule">Proof, simulation and physical correspondence retain distinct evidence status. Physical promotion: 0.</p></footer></div></body></html>
