+<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Unified Dynamics public research atlas: finite tetrahedral mathematics, declared dynamics, source provenance and independently testable physical questions."><meta name="theme-color" content="#f7f6ef"><title>History comparison · Unified Dynamics</title><link rel="icon" href="/assets/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/style.css"><script src="/assets/app.js" defer></script></head><body data-page="history-comparison"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><aside class="sidebar"><a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 3L3 33H37Z M20 3L22 23L3 33 M22 23L37 33"/></svg><div>Unified<br>Dynamics<small>PUBLIC RESEARCH ATLAS</small></div></a><button class="menu-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="navigation">Explore <span>☰</span></button><nav id="navigation" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/" ><span>01</span>Overview</a><a href="/primer/" ><span>02</span>Primer</a><a href="/mathematics/" ><span>03</span>Mathematics</a><a href="/dynamics/" ><span>04</span>Dynamics</a><a href="/evidence/" ><span>05</span>Evidence</a><a href="/papers/" ><span>06</span>Papers</a><a href="/sources/" ><span>07</span>Sources</a><a href="/history/" ><span>08</span>History</a><a href="/contribution/" ><span>09</span>Contribution</a><a href="/updates/" ><span>10</span>Updates</a><a href="/reconciliation/"><span>11</span>Reconciliation</a><a href="/dependencies/"><span>12</span>Dependencies</a><a href="/source-contract/"><span>13</span>Source contract</a><a href="/source-programme/"><span>14</span>Source programme</a><a href="/realization/"><span>15</span>Realization</a><a href="/joint-carrier/"><span>16</span>Joint carrier</a><a href="/programmed-clock/"><span>17</span>Programmed clock</a><a href="/native-admission/"><span>18</span>Native admission</a><a href="/metric-admission/"><span>19</span>Source metrics</a><a href="/subdivision/"><span>20</span>Subdivision</a><a href="/metric-selection/"><span>21</span>Metric selection</a><a href="/refinement-tower/"><span>22</span>Refinement tower</a><a href="/history-comparison/" aria-current="page"><span>23</span>History comparison</a><a href="/observation/"><span>24</span>Observation</a></nav><div class="sidebar-bottom"><span class="status-dot"></span> Physical promotion <b>0</b><p>Independent human review<br>pending</p><a href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD">Research repository ↗</a></div></aside><div class="page-shell"><header class="topbar"><span>FINITE STRUCTURE / OPEN CORRESPONDENCE</span><a href="/sources/">Search the record <span>⌕</span></a></header><main id="main"><div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">History comparison v0.1 · development</div><h1>Same coarse code. Different retained histories.</h1><p class="lede">A center-star and a barycentric refinement preserve the old tetrahedron. Matching frequencies permits an unrestricted encoding, but preserving vertex symmetry forbids that complete encoding under the declared metrics.</p></div><aside class="callout"><strong>Conditional comparison · native source law open</strong><p>All results use affine retractions, unit-detail calibration and a fixed internal rate. No physical promotion; independent human review pending. These claims do not select the native metric or refinement event.</p></aside>
 <section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">01</div><div><h2>Compare every retained direction</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Carrier</th><th>Total directions</th><th>Details</th><th>√5 detail pairs</th><th>S4-trivial √5 pairs</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Original tetrahedron</td><td>15</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>Center-star 1→4</td><td>29</td><td>14</td><td>7</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>Barycentric</td><td>149</td><td>134</td><td>10</td><td>0</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The common coarse code retains seven frequency2 pairs and one harmonic direction. The star adds seven √5 pairs. Barycentric has enough matching frequencies, but none of its √5 modes is invariant under all24 original vertex permutations.</p><p>These spectra belong to H=RᵀR+QᵀQ, Q=I−SR and the corresponding weighted generator. They are not raw unit-metric fine spectra.</p></div></section>
 <section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">02</div><div><h2>Which notion of equivalence?</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Comparison</th><th>Result</th><th>What it retains</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Coarse transfer SsRb</td><td>Exact, but lossy</td><td>Old15 directions; kills134 barycentric details</td></tr><tr><td>Full terminal bijection</td><td>NO-GO</td><td>Dimensions29 and149 differ</td></tr><tr><td>Star→bary generator embedding</td><td>Exists without symmetry</td><td>All29 source directions; nonunique spectral encoding</td></tr><tr><td>S4-equivariant generator embedding</td><td>NO-GO under this contract</td><td>Required invariant √5 pair is absent from target</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>A comparison must preserve both the stated dynamics and the required symmetry representation. Frequency counts alone do not establish history covariance. Changing metrics, rates, symmetry demands or adding carriers requires a new test.</p></div></section>
 <section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>Keep the outgoing record</h2><p>A reversible transfer can retain all data by adding14 target-detail directions and keeping134 old-detail directions as an outgoing record.</p><div class="callout"><p class="form">149 input +14 prepared →29 target +134 record =163 directions</p><p>(Sb c+zb, ws) →(Ss c+ws, zb)</p></div><p>Both sides have squared norm ||c||²+||zb||²+||ws||². With blank ws=0, the old detail record still exists. This is an information-preserving direct-sum transfer, not an acquired clock, physical gate, complete generator equivalence or free reset.</p></div></section>
