-<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Unified Dynamics public research atlas: finite tetrahedral mathematics, declared dynamics, source provenance and independently testable physical questions."><meta name="theme-color" content="#f7f6ef"><title>History · Unified Dynamics</title><link rel="icon" href="/assets/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/style.css"><script src="/assets/app.js" defer></script></head><body data-page="history"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><aside class="sidebar"><a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 3L3 33H37Z M20 3L22 23L3 33 M22 23L37 33"/></svg><div>Unified<br>Dynamics<small>PUBLIC RESEARCH ATLAS</small></div></a><button class="menu-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="navigation">Explore <span>☰</span></button><nav id="navigation" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/" ><span>01</span>Overview</a><a href="/primer/" ><span>02</span>Primer</a><a href="/mathematics/" ><span>03</span>Mathematics</a><a href="/dynamics/" ><span>04</span>Dynamics</a><a href="/evidence/" ><span>05</span>Evidence</a><a href="/papers/" ><span>06</span>Papers</a><a href="/sources/" ><span>07</span>Sources</a><a href="/history/" aria-current="page"><span>08</span>History</a><a href="/contribution/" ><span>09</span>Contribution</a><a href="/updates/" ><span>10</span>Updates</a><a href="/reconciliation/"><span>11</span>Reconciliation</a><a href="/dependencies/"><span>12</span>Dependencies</a><a href="/source-contract/"><span>13</span>Source contract</a><a href="/source-programme/"><span>14</span>Source programme</a><a href="/realization/"><span>15</span>Realization</a><a href="/joint-carrier/"><span>16</span>Joint carrier</a><a href="/programmed-clock/"><span>17</span>Programmed clock</a><a href="/native-admission/"><span>18</span>Native admission</a><a href="/metric-admission/"><span>19</span>Source metrics</a><a href="/subdivision/"><span>20</span>Subdivision</a><a href="/metric-selection/"><span>21</span>Metric selection</a><a href="/refinement-tower/"><span>22</span>Refinement tower</a><a href="/history-comparison/"><span>23</span>History comparison</a></nav><div class="sidebar-bottom"><span class="status-dot"></span> Physical promotion <b>0</b><p>Independent human review<br>pending</p><a href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD">Research repository ↗</a></div></aside><div class="page-shell"><header class="topbar"><span>FINITE STRUCTURE / OPEN CORRESPONDENCE</span><a href="/sources/">Search the record <span>⌕</span></a></header><main id="main"><div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">Lineage and corrections</div><h1>Keep the past visible. Keep its status explicit.</h1><p class="lede">Historical proposals explain how the programme developed. Their confidence language is not automatically inherited by the current presentation.</p></div><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">01</div><div><h2>The programme’s generations.</h2><div class="timeline"><div><span>Early 2026</span><h3>Distinction Theory / Distinction Dynamics</h3><p>Packet-routing, seam holonomy, coherence, matter and cosmology proposals. Several supplied equation snapshots are placeholders.</p></div><div><span>May 2026</span><h3>Unified Dynamics v2.2–v2.3</h3><p>Broad parameter-free physics and capacity claims. Preserved as historical proposals pending a lawful source-to-measurement derivation.</p></div><div><span>August–September 2026</span><h3>Typed ledgers and finite-carrier audits</h3><p>Exact internal statements, conditional branches, no-gos and source gaps are separated.</p></div><div><span>October 2026</span><h3>Consolidated papers and source gates</h3><p>Review papers plus amendments on event eligibility, interfaces, signature and receipt resource costs.</p></div></div><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=S03">S03 ↗</a> <a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=S04">S04 ↗</a> <a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=A20">A20 ↗</a> <a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=PI">PI ↗</a></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">02</div><div><h2>Versioned dispositions.</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Earlier statement</th><th>Current disposition</th><th>Reopening condition</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Equation pages / full repository supply complete derivations</td><td>9 standalone placeholders and 55 ZIP placeholders</td><td>Recover original equations and runnable sources</td></tr><tr><td>g = EδEᵀ derives Lorentzian spacetime for real E, positive δ</td><td>NO-GO on that carrier: the form is positive semidefinite</td><td>Source-derived hyperbolic co-metric on a separately typed carrier</td></tr><tr><td>Gap 2 gives a parameter-free measured spectral index</td><td>Historical report itself retains an undetermined n_CMB; replay unavailable</td><td>Original code/data, scale convention, running-sign repair and held-out evaluation</td></tr><tr><td>K₄ / S₄ counts derive Standard Model groups and measured constants</td><td>Historical physical identifications quarantined</td><td>Valid group/carrier map, dynamics, normalization and independent bridge</td></tr><tr><td>Later O45 ledger says sidecar not distributed</td><td>October 13 audit records conflicting later sent-message evidence; scorer bytes still missing</td><td>Preserve old row; consult amendment; recover original hash-matching bytes</td></tr><tr><td>34-slot write plus 32 storage rounds fits a 44-slot deadline</td><td>Correct schedule is 66 slots</td><td>Compare equal deadlines or equal storage ages explicitly</td></tr></tbody></table></div><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=A14">A14 · §§1, 4 ↗</a> <a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=R30">R30 · coframe conflict §3 ↗</a> <a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=R35">R35 · distribution conflict ↗</a> <a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=R40">R40 · clock ↗</a></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>Numbers retain their types.</h2><p>7/768, 960/7, 1/(9π²), fitted spectral indices and the historical target 238.14 appear in older research. A count, a normalized ratio, a fitted parameter and a measured physical constant are different objects. Numerical agreement cannot supply the missing constitutive law or unit map.</p><p>The current ledger distinguishes exact internal objects, conditional results, candidates and frozen uses. The public atlas does not rederive a historical constant by backsolving its desired value.</p><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=S04">S04 · historical capacity and gauge claims ↗</a> <a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=L65">L65 ↗</a> <a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=M01">M01 · item 12 ↗</a></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">04</div><div><h2>Original inputs remain recoverable.</h2><p>The source registry includes every available attachment, both historical URLs, current portal records and the pinned GitHub file inventory. Raw notebooks are cataloged with hashes and scientific topics; internal and patent material is not republished. The missing genesis image remains an explicit intake gap.</p><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?group=Attached%20sources">Inspect the intake record →</a></div></section></main><footer><div><a href="/">Unified Dynamics</a><p>Benjamin Walker Mayes · Independent researcher<br>AI-assisted research · Public reading edition 0.14</p></div><div><a href="/sources/">Sources & coverage</a><a href="/contribution/">Contribution</a><a href="https://tetrahedral-packet-complexes.ben-w-mayes.chatgpt.site/">Living research portal ↗</a></div><p class="footer-rule">Proof, simulation and physical correspondence retain distinct evidence status. Physical promotion: 0.</p></footer></div></body></html>
