-<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Unified Dynamics public research atlas: finite tetrahedral mathematics, declared dynamics, source provenance and independently testable physical questions."><meta name="theme-color" content="#f7f6ef"><title>Mathematics · Unified Dynamics</title><link rel="icon" href="/assets/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/style.css"><script src="/assets/app.js" defer></script></head><body data-page="mathematics"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><aside class="sidebar"><a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 3L3 33H37Z M20 3L22 23L3 33 M22 23L37 33"/></svg><div>Unified<br>Dynamics<small>PUBLIC RESEARCH ATLAS</small></div></a><button class="menu-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="navigation">Explore <span>☰</span></button><nav id="navigation" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/" ><span>01</span>Overview</a><a href="/primer/" ><span>02</span>Primer</a><a href="/mathematics/" aria-current="page"><span>03</span>Mathematics</a><a href="/dynamics/" ><span>04</span>Dynamics</a><a href="/evidence/" ><span>05</span>Evidence</a><a href="/papers/" ><span>06</span>Papers</a><a href="/sources/" ><span>07</span>Sources</a><a href="/history/" ><span>08</span>History</a><a href="/contribution/" ><span>09</span>Contribution</a><a href="/updates/" ><span>10</span>Updates</a><a href="/reconciliation/"><span>11</span>Reconciliation</a><a href="/dependencies/"><span>12</span>Dependencies</a><a href="/source-contract/"><span>13</span>Source contract</a><a href="/source-programme/"><span>14</span>Source programme</a><a href="/realization/"><span>15</span>Realization</a><a href="/joint-carrier/"><span>16</span>Joint carrier</a><a href="/programmed-clock/"><span>17</span>Programmed clock</a><a href="/native-admission/"><span>18</span>Native admission</a><a href="/metric-admission/"><span>19</span>Source metrics</a><a href="/subdivision/"><span>20</span>Subdivision</a><a href="/metric-selection/"><span>21</span>Metric selection</a><a href="/refinement-tower/"><span>22</span>Refinement tower</a><a href="/history-comparison/"><span>23</span>History comparison</a></nav><div class="sidebar-bottom"><span class="status-dot"></span> Physical promotion <b>0</b><p>Independent human review<br>pending</p><a href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD">Research repository ↗</a></div></aside><div class="page-shell"><header class="topbar"><span>FINITE STRUCTURE / OPEN CORRESPONDENCE</span><a href="/sources/">Search the record <span>⌕</span></a></header><main id="main"><div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">Scoped results</div><h1>The mathematical core.</h1><p class="lede">Results are stated on declared carriers and metrics. A finite theorem retains its assumptions when it enters a larger programme.</p></div><div class="claims-grid"><article class="claim" id="ATLAS01"><div class="claim-top"><span class="mono">ATLAS01</span><span class="tag exact">EXACT / SCOPED</span></div><h3>Filled-tetrahedron flow</h3><p class="premise">Increasing-order orientation, unit Euclidean simplex basis, A = Bᵀ − B.</p><div class="claim-result">A² = −4(I − P₀); det(λI − A) = λ(λ² + 4)⁷. One harmonic vertex mode and seven conjugate pairs ±2i.</div><p class="muted">No physical frequency or time unit follows.</p><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=PI">PI · §4.3 ↗</a></article><article class="claim" id="ATLAS02"><div class="claim-top"><span class="mono">ATLAS02</span><span class="tag exact">EXACT / SCOPED</span></div><h3>Glued-carrier spectra</h3><p class="premise">Unique simplices on the specified two- and three-tetrahedron complexes.</p><div class="claim-result">K₋: λ(λ² + 3)⁴(λ² + 5)⁷. K₊: λ(λ² + 2)²(λ² + 5)¹¹.</div><p class="muted">Irrational active-frequency ratios prohibit a full-operator common period; special single-frequency states can still recur.</p><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=PI">PI · §6.3 ↗</a></article><article class="claim" id="ATLAS03"><div class="claim-top"><span class="mono">ATLAS03</span><span class="tag exact">EXACT / SCOPED</span></div><h3>Common ambient comparison</h3><p class="premise">The labeled 2↔3 move is compared in the 30-dimensional boundary of Δ⁴.</p><div class="claim-result">The operator difference has rank 18 and kernel dimension 12. The specified chain, isometry and boundary-fixing requirements conflict.</div><p class="muted">Changing the metric or jump contract defines a different branch.</p><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=PI">PI · §6.5 ↗</a></article><article class="claim" id="ATLAS04"><div class="claim-top"><span class="mono">ATLAS04</span><span class="tag exact">EXACT / SCOPED</span></div><h3>Signed S₄ commutant</h3><p class="premise">Signed action on the full graded filled-tetrahedron chain carrier.</p><div class="claim-result">Equivariant commutant dimension 13; self-adjoint part 10; skew-adjoint part 3.</div><p class="muted">Finite permutation symmetry is not a derivation of Standard Model gauge groups.</p><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=PIII">PIII · §2.3 ↗</a></article><article class="claim" id="ATLAS05"><div class="claim-top"><span class="mono">ATLAS05</span><span class="tag exact">EXACT / CONDITIONAL</span></div><h3>Projective reconstruction</h3><p class="premise">Valid normalized stocks, forest incidence receipts and one root reference per nonzero-support component.</p><div class="claim-result">Real signs or complex phases reconstruct the normalized state under the corresponding source convention.</div><p class="muted">Missing component references leave ambiguity; real-part currents alone do not supply all complex phases.</p><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=PII">PII · §§3, 6 ↗</a></article><article class="claim" id="ATLAS06"><div class="claim-top"><span class="mono">ATLAS06</span><span class="tag exact">EXACT / SCOPED</span></div><h3>Glued support ownership</h3><p class="premise">Global unique-simplex chains, supplied closed skew dynamics, equal top-star sharing.</p><div class="claim-result">Local incidence balance and cell ownership sum to the global support stock.</div><p class="muted">Open-system source terms and physical identification are separate.</p><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=PI">PI · §5 ↗</a></article><article class="claim" id="ATLAS07"><div class="claim-top"><span class="mono">ATLAS07</span><span class="tag ">DERIVED / CONDITIONAL</span></div><h3>Prepared finite controllers</h3><p class="premise">Supplied Hilbert spaces, Hamiltonians, initial resources, capture and matched renewal contracts.</p><div class="claim-result">Finite history words, capture windows and correlation export admit scoped bounds.</div><p class="muted">No permanent autonomous memory, native preparation or fully renewed physical cycle is established.</p><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=PIV">PIV · §§3–9 ↗</a></article></div><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">08</div><div><h2>One tetrahedron recurs. Glued carriers need not.</h2><div class="equation">eˢᴬ = P₀ + cos(2s)(I − P₀) + ½ sin(2s)A</div><p>The filled-cell full-operator period is π in the declared internal parameter. K₋ and K₊ have incommensurate active frequencies; there is no finite common period for the full operator.</p><div class="comparison"><div><span>Δ³</span><b>2</b><small>one active frequency</small></div><div><span>K₋</span><b>√3, √5</b><small>two incommensurate frequencies</small></div><div><span>K₊</span><b>√2, √5</b><small>two incommensurate frequencies</small></div></div><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=PI">PI · §§4.3, 6.4 ↗</a></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">09</div><div><h2>Trace the coefficients.</h2><p>The attached v0.39 ledger and later portal v0.65 file are preserved as distinct objects. Browse the later ledger’s 448 rows with their original bins, status, and next gates. A