+<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Unified Dynamics public research atlas: finite tetrahedral mathematics, declared dynamics, source provenance and independently testable physical questions."><meta name="theme-color" content="#f7f6ef"><title>Observation · Unified Dynamics</title><link rel="icon" href="/assets/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/style.css"><script src="/assets/app.js" defer></script></head><body data-page="observation"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><aside class="sidebar"><a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 3L3 33H37Z M20 3L22 23L3 33 M22 23L37 33"/></svg><div>Unified<br>Dynamics<small>PUBLIC RESEARCH ATLAS</small></div></a><button class="menu-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="navigation">Explore <span>☰</span></button><nav id="navigation" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/"><span>01</span>Overview</a><a href="/primer/" ><span>02</span>Primer</a><a href="/mathematics/" ><span>03</span>Mathematics</a><a href="/dynamics/" ><span>04</span>Dynamics</a><a href="/evidence/" ><span>05</span>Evidence</a><a href="/papers/" ><span>06</span>Papers</a><a href="/sources/" ><span>07</span>Sources</a><a href="/history/" ><span>08</span>History</a><a href="/contribution/" ><span>09</span>Contribution</a><a href="/updates/" ><span>10</span>Updates</a><a href="/reconciliation/"><span>11</span>Reconciliation</a><a href="/dependencies/"><span>12</span>Dependencies</a><a href="/source-contract/"><span>13</span>Source contract</a><a href="/source-programme/"><span>14</span>Source programme</a><a href="/realization/"><span>15</span>Realization</a><a href="/joint-carrier/"><span>16</span>Joint carrier</a><a href="/programmed-clock/"><span>17</span>Programmed clock</a><a href="/native-admission/"><span>18</span>Native admission</a><a href="/metric-admission/"><span>19</span>Source metrics</a><a href="/subdivision/"><span>20</span>Subdivision</a><a href="/metric-selection/"><span>21</span>Metric selection</a><a href="/refinement-tower/"><span>22</span>Refinement tower</a><a href="/history-comparison/"><span>23</span>History comparison</a><a href="/observation/" aria-current="page"><span>24</span>Observation</a></nav><div class="sidebar-bottom"><span class="status-dot"></span> Physical promotion <b>0</b><p>Independent human review<br>pending</p><a href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD">Research repository ↗</a></div></aside><div class="page-shell"><header class="topbar"><span>FINITE STRUCTURE / OPEN CORRESPONDENCE</span><a href="/sources/">Search the record <span>⌕</span></a></header><main id="main"><div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">16–17 October 2026 · Observation session</div><h1>What can a shell reveal?</h1><p class="lede">Concrete 600-cell readouts, finite calibration and spectral extraction with a bounded memory footprint.</p><p>These results concern declared finite mathematical models and constructor-side verification. The public record contains 26 research packages/captures: 17 earlier archives recovered intact and nine later captures. No apparatus measurements or physical identification are established.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/blob/9d5f9f354d36b8528fa20c86d7837d18d0edee1f/captures/2026-10-17T184000Z-codex-session-publication-7f4a2d91/README.md">Complete session record ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/pull/179">Merged evidence · PR #179 ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/users/ud-tetra/projects/1/views/1?pane=info&amp;statusUpdateId=289526">Project progress ↗</a></div></div><aside class="callout"><strong>Development — no registry entry · Physical promotion 0</strong><p>Independent scientific review is on HOLD. Repository integration, numerical certification and lossless record encoding have separate scopes.</p></aside><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href="#shells">Shells</a><a class="text-link" href="#sectors">Sectors</a><a class="text-link" href="#calibration">Calibration</a><a class="text-link" href="#spectra">Memory-limited extraction</a><a class="text-link" href="#review">Review gates</a><a class="text-link" href="#record">All 26 sources</a></div><section class="chapter" id="shells"><div class="chapter-label">01</div><div><h2>A different observer changes the kernel.</h2><p>The regular 600-cell boundary is a closed 3-sphere with chain dimensions (120, 720, 1200, 600), total 2640. A selected vertex link is an icosahedral 2-sphere with 62 simplex coordinates. It is the boundary of a vertex star, not the manifold boundary of the whole 3-sphere.</p><p>Fix the real, unit-metric, unweighted skew Hodge–Dirac generator. Ideal history uses every derivative of the selected signed simplex amplitudes. Its unobservable space is the intersection of the kernels of R A<sup>k</sup>; a snapshot kernel alone does not give the dynamical answer.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Readout</th><th scope="col">Channels</th><th scope="col">Ideal history rank</th><th scope="col">Hidden dimensions</th><th scope="col">Sufficient finite conditioning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>One link: centre 0</td><td>62</td><td>1893</td><td>747</td><td>The later 37-preparation Hankel protocol has its own signal bound.</td></tr><tr><td>Second link: centre 45, plus tetrahedron (0,33,34,41)</td><td>125</td><td>2498</td><td>142</td><td>8192 samples, step 1/2; condition &lt;1183 on the observable subspace.</td></tr><tr><td>Three links: centres 0,45,66; tetrahedron and three extra simplex ports</td><td>189</td><td>2640</td><td>0</td><td>8192 samples: condition &lt;296; 2048 samples: &lt;725.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The second configuration removes 605 of the original 747 hidden dimensions. The third exposes the remaining 142. These are different observers: the original 62-channel system still cannot see dynamics confined to its invariant 747-dimensional kernel. Bounds refer to normalized finite sample maps in model time, not calibrated physical instruments.</p></div></section><section class="chapter" id="sectors"><div class="chapter-label">02</div><div><h2>Sector ranks do not add across this readout.</h2><p>Each complex C<sub>10</sub> character sector has dimension 264. The single-link readout has isolated-sector snapshot rank 51. Its history ranks are:</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Character index m</th><th scope="col">Isolated-sector history rank</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>0</td><td>255</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>220</td></tr><tr><td>1, 3, 7, 9</td><td>254</td></tr><tr><td>2, 4, 6, 8</td><td>258</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The chosen readout does not intertwine the C<sub>10</sub> action. Summing these isolated-sector ranks therefore does not give the full rank 1893.</p><p>Coefficient fields matter. The characteristic-13 calculation has observation rank 1877 and a 763-dimensional kernel, separately from the real result. The irreducible cubic x³−2 and quartic Φ<sub>10</sub> define a degree-12 compositum; this exact field arithmetic does not transfer real singular-value conditioning or set a Pachner recurrence period.</p></div></section><section class="chapter" id="calibration"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>Finite accuracy needs a declared error contract.</h2><p>The finite six-ratio protocol uses three known preparations, 12 scalar readings at h=1/32 and 20 projected inversion iterations. Under its stated bounded error assumptions, the tracking bound is below 6.189×10<sup>−13</sup>, hence below 2<sup>−40</sup> and the requested 2<sup>−39</sup> gate. This is a conditional mathematical certificate, not empirical calibration.</p><p>The linked packages separately address gain/rate/clock ambiguity, grade metrics, fitted-coordinate transfer, held-out discrepancy, local fault detection and the precision versus measurement-count frontier. The optimized restricted diagnostic protocol uses 493,290 readings at response error 2<sup>−58</sup>; a stricter variant uses 394,632 at 2<sup>−64</sup>. Their hypotheses and intermediate error targets differ.</p><p>The proposed random-matrix self-prediction script and Euler stepping are not held-out model validation. The 2<sup>−49</sup> residual gate is unsupported and rejected. The 2<sup>−38</sup> shape gate retains its typed calibration meaning; it is not a Borel-shear allowance.</p></div></section><section class="chapter" id="spectra"><div class="chapter-label">04</div><div><h2>Extract the spectrum without the 287-GiB array.</h2><p>A single freely evolving trajectory has at most 105 temporal directions in this model. Adding Hankel columns alone cannot excite 1893 independent observable directions. The explicit 2640×37 preparation matrix supplies the required modal excitation; each preparation has squared norm 165/169.</p><p>The frozen primary record uses M=4096, 8191 temporal vectors per preparation and 62 history channels: <strong>18,790,154 scalar readings</strong>. Its normalized Hankel matrix has shape 253952×151552; binary64 dense storage would use 286.75 GiB. Exact Hankel actions, energy accounting, verified 1893×1893 factor Grams and projection residual bounds avoid that allocation.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Frozen nominal benchmark</th><th scope="col">Verified outcome</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Retained singular values above the frozen threshold</td><td>1893</td></tr><tr><td>Condition enclosure</td><td>&lt;706.570 (sufficient family ceiling: 2029)</td></tr><tr><td>Nominal projection Frobenius tail</td><td>&lt;9.615×10⁻¹⁴</td></tr><tr><td>Record-only complete tail</td><td>&lt;1.132×10⁻¹²</td></tr><tr><td>Nominal sequential run</td><td>152.85 seconds; maximum worker RSS 2.725 GiB</td></tr><tr><td>Record-only verification</td><td>112.87 seconds; maximum worker RSS 1.99206 GiB</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The nominal benchmark uses known modal factors. The later record-only proposer learns 105 temporal components from the record and contract, while the verifier checks all readings against the proposed model. The timing and worker-memory figures describe those frozen runs, not a universal performance guarantee. The 62 history channels remain distinct from the 189 diagnostic outputs and additional calibration ports.</p></div></section><section class="chapter" id="noise"><div class="chapter-label">05</div><div><h2>Bounded noisy examples pass a narrower test.</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Full-size noisy record</th><th scope="col">Condition enclosure</th><th scope="col">Complete tail upper bound</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Dense signs</td><td>&lt;747.128</td><td>6.470×10⁻⁶</td></tr><tr><td>Coherent DC</td><td>&lt;752.797</td><td>7.320×10⁻⁶</td></tr><tr><td>Ramp</td><td>&lt;724.387</td><td>2.932×10⁻⁶</td></tr><tr><td>Single vector</td><td>&lt;706.664</td><td>1.582×10⁻⁸</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>All four certify 1893 singular values above the unchanged threshold. The temporal sketch theorem separates 105 components throughout the declared per-vector 2<sup>−20</sup> additive error ball. It does not establish universal frequency-fitting or optimizer convergence, or full calibration-family robustness. The single-vector fixture meets the vector ceiling but exceeds the sufficient scalar ceiling; no full acquisition-contract membership follows.</p><p><strong>Threshold count is not exact algebraic rank.</strong> A certified weak impulse record has rank at least 2203 while retaining only 1893 singular values above threshold. The codec recovers every byte of the finite recorded history by retaining residuals. It does not reconstruct hidden bulk state or select a unique continuous-time generator through sampling aliases.</p></div></section><section class="chapter" id="corrections"><div class="chapter-label">06</div><div><h2>The parallel-work corrections remain visible.</h2><ul class="checklist"><li>A coframe or a chosen right inverse selects a lift; it cannot recover an arbitrary discarded kernel without additional information.</li><li>Boundary nilpotency does not impose coframe torsion flatness. A Pachner move needs typed incidence/coframe compatibility, not an automatic flatness-violation claim for an undefined edge value.</li><li>The supplied Q₈ matrices over F₁₃ can be verified exactly. The claimed embedding 2I into SL(2,F₁₃) cannot hold: 120 does not divide 2184. No unsupported C₁₃ or dihedral branching rule is promoted.</li><li>Twenty incident tetrahedra do not define a self-similar fractal or a Hausdorff dimension above its embedding dimension.</li><li>Finite fields, geometric frames, norm conservation, clocks and physical gauge groups require separate definitions and correspondence evidence.</li></ul><p>The source audits preserve valid finite arithmetic and counterexamples while separating them from unsupported gauge, curvature and leakage interpretations.</p></div></section><section class="chapter" id="review"><div class="chapter-label">07</div><div><h2>Review is a source-bound return.</h2><aside class="callout"><strong>Independent review: HOLD</strong><p>Each supplied review manifest mismatches all 12 existing target-package file hashes. Original review-file bytes and attributable reviewer independence were not supplied. A different revision is possible; no intent is inferred.</p></aside><p>A corrected return must identify the exact archive or commit, provide matching hashes, declare reviewer identity and independence, distinguish static inspection from fresh execution, and state scoped pass/fail/open findings. Constructor/verifier software separation alone does not establish independent human review.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Task</th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">Next gate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/issues/176">Completed computational record #176</a></td><td>Done</td><td>Bounded task complete; PR #179 merged.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/issues/177">Independent review #177</a></td><td>Blocked / HOLD</td><td>Attributable, hash-bound corrected return.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/issues/178">Broader noisy fitting #178</a></td><td>Ready</td><td>Independent records, convergence/failure domain and residual guarantees.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/issues/136">Metric and observer selection #136</a></td><td>Open</td><td>Native selecting premises or explicit residual freedom.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/issues/144">Acquisition qualification #144</a></td><td>Open</td><td>Metrology, timing, dependence, preparation/disturbance and costs.</td></tr><tr><td><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD/issues/130">Independent replay #130</a></td><td>Open</td><td>Pinned environment, named replays and negative controls.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>All work remains in the development lane. Neither a task marked Done, a merged repository PR nor this public update enacts scientific or physical promotion.</p></div></section><section class="chapter" id="record"><div class="chapter-label">08</div><div><h2>Inspect every part of the session.</h2><p>The earlier 17 archives were recovered after the transient checkout was lost. ZIP checks and all 307 original manifest entries passed during repository publication. Those scientific receipts are inherited; they were not all replayed during recovery. The nine later captures retain their own exact/numerical verification scopes.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Research package / capture</th><th scope="col">Provenance</th><th scope="