-<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Unified Dynamics public research atlas: finite tetrahedral mathematics, declared dynamics, source provenance and independently testable physical questions."><meta name="theme-color" content="#f7f6ef"><title>Primer · Unified Dynamics</title><link rel="icon" href="/assets/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/style.css"><script src="/assets/app.js" defer></script></head><body data-page="primer"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><aside class="sidebar"><a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 3L3 33H37Z M20 3L22 23L3 33 M22 23L37 33"/></svg><div>Unified<br>Dynamics<small>PUBLIC RESEARCH ATLAS</small></div></a><button class="menu-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="navigation">Explore <span>☰</span></button><nav id="navigation" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/" ><span>01</span>Overview</a><a href="/primer/" aria-current="page"><span>02</span>Primer</a><a href="/mathematics/" ><span>03</span>Mathematics</a><a href="/dynamics/" ><span>04</span>Dynamics</a><a href="/evidence/" ><span>05</span>Evidence</a><a href="/papers/" ><span>06</span>Papers</a><a href="/sources/" ><span>07</span>Sources</a><a href="/history/" ><span>08</span>History</a><a href="/contribution/" ><span>09</span>Contribution</a><a href="/updates/" ><span>10</span>Updates</a><a href="/reconciliation/"><span>11</span>Reconciliation</a><a href="/dependencies/"><span>12</span>Dependencies</a><a href="/source-contract/"><span>13</span>Source contract</a><a href="/source-programme/"><span>14</span>Source programme</a><a href="/realization/"><span>15</span>Realization</a><a href="/joint-carrier/"><span>16</span>Joint carrier</a><a href="/programmed-clock/"><span>17</span>Programmed clock</a><a href="/native-admission/"><span>18</span>Native admission</a><a href="/metric-admission/"><span>19</span>Source metrics</a><a href="/subdivision/"><span>20</span>Subdivision</a><a href="/metric-selection/"><span>21</span>Metric selection</a><a href="/refinement-tower/"><span>22</span>Refinement tower</a><a href="/history-comparison/"><span>23</span>History comparison</a></nav><div class="sidebar-bottom"><span class="status-dot"></span> Physical promotion <b>0</b><p>Independent human review<br>pending</p><a href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD">Research repository ↗</a></div></aside><div class="page-shell"><header class="topbar"><span>FINITE STRUCTURE / OPEN CORRESPONDENCE</span><a href="/sources/">Search the record <span>⌕</span></a></header><main id="main"><div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">Start here</div><h1>From structure to a testable question.</h1><p class="lede">A short guide to the objects UD uses, and the boundaries between geometry, dynamics and physics.</p></div><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">01</div><div><h2>A graph is not a filled cell.</h2><p>The complete graph K₄ has four vertices and six edges. The <strong>filled tetrahedron Δ³</strong> adds four triangular faces and one 3-cell. Its graded chain space therefore has 15 real amplitude coordinates.</p><div class="explorer"><div><svg class="tetra" viewBox="0 0 480 390" role="img" aria-labelledby="tetra-title"><title id="tetra-title">A filled tetrahedron: four vertices, six edges, four faces and one cell</title><defs><pattern id="grid" width="30" height="30" patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M30 0H0V30" fill="none" stroke="#dddcd3" stroke-width=".6"/></pattern></defs><rect x="0" y="0" width="480" height="390" fill="url(#grid)"/><g class="tetra-body"><path d="M240 50L65 290L415 290L265 200Z" fill="#bcd1c9" opacity=".18"/></g><g class="tetra-faces" fill="#aac9c0" stroke="#417569" stroke-width="1"><path d="M240 50L65 290L265 200Z" opacity=".25"/><path d="M240 50L415 290L265 200Z" opacity=".35"/><path d="M65 290L415 290L265 200Z" opacity=".30"/></g><g class="tetra-edges" fill="none" stroke="#356d61" stroke-width="2"><path d="M240 50L65 290L415 290Z M240 50L265 200"/><path d="M65 290L265 200L415 290" stroke-dasharray="6 5"/></g><g class="tetra-vertices" fill="#183e36"><circle cx="240" cy="50" r="7"/><circle cx="65" cy="290" r="7"/><circle cx="415" cy="290" r="7"/><circle cx="265" cy="200" r="7"/></g><g fill="#183e36" font-family="monospace" font-size="14"><text x="250" y="37">0</text><text x="42" y="314">1</text><text x="426" y="314">2</text><text x="276" y="194">3</text></g><text x="24" y="370" fill="#61736c" font-family="monospace" font-size="11">SCHEMATIC GEOMETRY · NO PHYSICAL LENGTH SCALE</text></svg></div><div><h3>Inspect a chain degree</h3><div class="degree-controls"><button data-degree="0" class="selected">C₀</button><button data-degree="1">C₁</button><button data-degree="2">C₂</button><button data-degree="3">C₃</button><button data-degree="all">All</button></div><p id="degree-description" aria-live="polite">C₀ stores four vertex amplitudes. Coordinate count does not identify four spacetime dimensions.</p><div class="big-number" id="degree-count">4 <small>coordinates</small></div></div></div><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=PI">PI · §§3–4 ↗</a></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">02</div><div><h2>Topology fixes a language. A generator fixes a motion.</h2><p>The boundary operator B takes an oriented simplex to its boundary. The identity B² = 0 means the boundary of a boundary vanishes. With an orthonormal simplex basis, UD studies the real skew generator A = Bᵀ − B.</p><div class="equation">c(s) ∈ C₀ ⊕ C₁ ⊕ C₂ ⊕ C₃ &nbsp; · &nbsp; dc/ds = Ac</div><p>Skew symmetry preserves the squared norm. Here s is a mathematical evolution parameter. Its relation to seconds, energy and laboratory readout requires a separate calibrated map.</p><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=PI">PI · §4 ↗</a></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>A conserved total can still flow locally.</h2><p>Adjacent chain coordinates exchange quadratic support through signed incidence currents. The total remains conserved in a closed fixed-carrier flow, while individual simplex stocks can rise or fall. Shared simplices are represented once; a shared face is an active reservoir.</p><div class="equation">S = ∑σ cσ² &nbsp; · &nbsp; Jστ = 2Bστ cσcτ</div><p>“Support” here means squared chain amplitude. It is not automatically mass, thermodynamic entropy or energy.</p><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=PI">PI · §5 ↗</a></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">04</div><div><h2>An observation can hide a state.</h2><p>Stocks discard signs and phases. Projective support receipts add signed or complex incidence information, plus the required component references, to reconstruct a normalized state. A valid reconstruction theorem depends on which observations were actually supplied.</p><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=PII">PII · §§2–6 ↗</a></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">05</div><div><h2>Persistence needs its own test.</h2><p>Agreement at one instant, retention over an interval, and preference for growing into a cluster are different observables. Prepared shells, memories and controllers can test conditional mechanisms. A source-selected shape law and a complete physical apparatus remain further questions.</p><a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=PIII">PIII · §§11–14 ↗</a> <a class="citation" href="/sources/?id=PIV">PIV · §§1, 9 ↗</a><aside class="callout"><strong>Next reading</strong><p>Read Mathematics for scoped results, Dynamics for the missing event laws, and Evidence for the physical bridge gates.</p></aside></div></section></main><footer><div><a href="/">Unified Dynamics</a><p>Benjamin Walker Mayes · Independent researcher<br>AI-assisted research · Public reading edition 0.14</p></div><div><a href="/sources/">Sources & coverage</a><a href="/contribution/">Contribution</a><a href="https://tetrahedral-packet-complexes.ben-w-mayes.chatgpt.site/">Living research portal ↗</a></div><p class="footer-rule">Proof, simulation and physical correspondence retain distinct evidence status. Physical promotion: 0.</p></footer></div></body></html>
