+<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="description" content="Unified Dynamics public research atlas: finite tetrahedral mathematics, declared dynamics, source provenance and independently testable physical questions."><meta name="theme-color" content="#f7f6ef"><title>Refinement tower · Unified Dynamics</title><link rel="icon" href="/assets/icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/style.css"><script src="/assets/app.js" defer></script><script src="/assets/refinement-tower-v0.1.js" defer></script></head><body data-page="refinement-tower"><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><aside class="sidebar"><a class="brand" href="/"><svg viewBox="0 0 40 40" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 3L3 33H37Z M20 3L22 23L3 33 M22 23L37 33"/></svg><div>Unified<br>Dynamics<small>PUBLIC RESEARCH ATLAS</small></div></a><button class="menu-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="navigation">Explore <span>☰</span></button><nav id="navigation" aria-label="Primary"><a href="/" ><span>01</span>Overview</a><a href="/primer/" ><span>02</span>Primer</a><a href="/mathematics/" ><span>03</span>Mathematics</a><a href="/dynamics/" ><span>04</span>Dynamics</a><a href="/evidence/" ><span>05</span>Evidence</a><a href="/papers/" ><span>06</span>Papers</a><a href="/sources/" ><span>07</span>Sources</a><a href="/history/" ><span>08</span>History</a><a href="/contribution/" ><span>09</span>Contribution</a><a href="/updates/" ><span>10</span>Updates</a><a href="/reconciliation/"><span>11</span>Reconciliation</a><a href="/dependencies/"><span>12</span>Dependencies</a><a href="/source-contract/"><span>13</span>Source contract</a><a href="/source-programme/"><span>14</span>Source programme</a><a href="/realization/"><span>15</span>Realization</a><a href="/joint-carrier/"><span>16</span>Joint carrier</a><a href="/programmed-clock/"><span>17</span>Programmed clock</a><a href="/native-admission/"><span>18</span>Native admission</a><a href="/metric-admission/"><span>19</span>Source metrics</a><a href="/subdivision/"><span>20</span>Subdivision</a><a href="/metric-selection/"><span>21</span>Metric selection</a><a href="/refinement-tower/" aria-current="page"><span>22</span>Refinement tower</a><a href="/history-comparison/"><span>23</span>History comparison</a><a href="/observation/"><span>24</span>Observation</a></nav><div class="sidebar-bottom"><span class="status-dot"></span> Physical promotion <b>0</b><p>Independent human review<br>pending</p><a href="https://github.com/ud-tetra/UD">Research repository ↗</a></div></aside><div class="page-shell"><header class="topbar"><span>FINITE STRUCTURE / OPEN CORRESPONDENCE</span><a href="/sources/">Search the record <span>⌕</span></a></header><main id="main"><div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">Refinement tower v0.1 · development</div><h1>Keep the calibration with the details.</h1><p class="lede">The one-step selector preserves the old code. Across two steps, inherited detail norms can change if the final complement receives fresh unit calibration. A retained hierarchy makes the same sequence consistent under regrouping.</p></div><aside class="callout"><strong>Exact conditional tower · source adoption open</strong><p>Both compared metrics preserve original coarse norm, boundary and dynamics. Their disagreement concerns retained details. The one-step theorem remains valid. Different refinement histories need separate comparison laws; physical promotion0.</p></aside>
 <section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">01</div><div><h2>Inspect the same retained detail state</h2><p>Choose two opposite oriented descendant contributions whose coarse retractions cancel. Its first-level squared norm is2. The second subdivision has degree-dependent Gram factors1,2,6,24.</p><div class="search-tools"><label>Detail degree<select id="rt-degree"><option value="1">Edge · degree1</option><option value="2">Face · degree2</option><option value="3">Cell · degree3</option></select></label></div><p id="rt-verdict" role="status"></p><div id="rt-witness"></div><p>Adding a coarse unit vertex leaves its absolute stock1 under both metrics. The normalized coarse fraction changes because the full retained denominator changes. These are exact quadratic receipts, not measured probabilities or instability bounds.</p></div></section>
 <section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">02</div><div><h2>Retain a hierarchy of calibrated components</h2><p>Write the final chain as x=S20c+S21z1+z2: old coarse state, inherited first-level detail and newest detail. The decoding maps are R20, Q10R21 and Q21. They reconstruct every final chain exactly.</p><div class="callout"><p class="form">||x||²=cᵀG0c+||z1||²+||z2||²</p><p>This is the sequential calibrated norm. A regrouped construction must transport both detail pairings. Replacing them with ||S21z1+z2||² is a fresh final-coordinate convention and generally changes the result.</p></div><p>The induced composite detail form is positive on the complement but semidefinite on the ambient space. It kills the original coarse image. Keeping that distinction makes the metric completion exact.</p><p>Coarse observable pullback composes exactly: K20=R21ᵀ(R10ᵀD_U R10)R21. It does not select the full detail metric. The complete sequential receipt has15 coarse outcomes plus two retained detail outcomes.</p></div></section>
 <section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>Count the whole retained carrier</h2><div class="search-tools"><label>Retained refinement levels<select id="rt-level"><option value="0">0</option><option value="1">1</option><option value="2" selected>2</option><option value="3">3</option><option value="4">4</option></select></label></div><div id="rt-counts"></div><p>Levels0–2 have explicitly regenerated sparse maps. Later rows are exact strict-flag counts; their full matrices are not built. At level2, the2745 directions contain15 coarse,134 inherited detail and2596 new detail directions.</p><p>These are direct-sum chain coordinates, not qubits or tensor donor banks. A finite whole-chain budget limits this full tower. New coordinates, clocks, preparation, readout and outgoing-record/reset resources need their own implementation.</p></div></section>
